From 9244482ab12953ffc6daf1bad825572e12de285b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:22:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] J604 local build: retry the automatic brightness default

Migration 1794108600 asked omarchy-brightness-auto for the default before
the package set shipped the service's unit, so install(1) could not find
/usr/share/omarchy/default/systemd/user/omarchy-brightness-auto.service.
Its "|| true" hid the error and omarchy-migrate marked it done, leaving a
machine with a built-in light sensor without automatic brightness.

omarchy-settings now ships the unit. Run the same default once more, without
ignoring a failure: a migration that cannot finish has to stay pending
(agents/skills/migrations.md).

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 migrations/1794122400.sh | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 migrations/1794122400.sh

diff --git a/migrations/1794122400.sh b/migrations/1794122400.sh
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..592bd24e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/migrations/1794122400.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+echo "Turn on automatic brightness for a built-in ambient light sensor"
+
+# 1794108600 ran before omarchy-settings shipped the service's unit, so the
+# default could not install it and the error was ignored. The unit ships now.
+# Same default: only with the machine's own light sensor, only if its user has
+# never turned automatic brightness on or off. A failure stays pending.
+omarchy-brightness-auto default
-- 
2.43.0

